\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "738a4e0cbcad33d280093808d8491a29f9b6bae5ddd19b897166250d0475262a"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Z"] ["math" "{0,\\,1}"] ["math" "{0}"] ["math" "{i}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-174447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-184610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let ${S}_{i}=[0+\\frac{1}{i},1],$ then ${⋃}_{i=3}^{\\infty }{S}_{i}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-184610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nThe notation ${⋃}_{i=3}^{\\infty }$ means that our set of indexes is \n${3,4,5…}.$ \n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${S}_{3}=[\\frac{1}{3},1]$\n\n- if $i=4,$ we have ${S}_{4}=[\\frac{1}{4},1]$\n\n- if $i=5,$ we have ${S}_{5}=[\\frac{1}{5},1]$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that as $i$ increases, \n\n- the left endpoint of the intervals approaches $0$ but never reaches it, and\n\n- the right endpoint of the intervals equals $1$ for all the sets.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i=3}^{\\infty }{S}_{i}=(0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-184610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "738a4e0cbcad33d280093808d8491a29f9b6bae5ddd19b897166250d0475262a"} {"question" "q-184610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-184610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,1]"] ["math" "[0,1]"] ["math" "[\\frac{1}{3},1]"] ["math" "{0}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-184610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,1]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-184654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let ${Y}_{i}=[-i,0],$ then ${⋃}_{i=3}^{\\infty }{Y}_{i}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/state.json" "file_sha256" "f66ce7d6be3334cff21aaca28820dbf192362f25e77804ff8388e910bd03ac52"} {"question" "q-184654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nThe notation ${⋃}_{i=3}^{\\infty }$ means that our set of indexes is \n${3,4,5…}.$ \n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${Y}_{3}=[-3,0]$\n\n- if $i=4,$ we have ${Y}_{4}=[-4,0]$\n\n- if $i=5,$ we have ${Y}_{5}=[-5,0]$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that as $i$ increases, \n\n- the sequence of left endpoints of the intervals approaches $-\\infty ,$ and\n\n- the right endpoint equals $0$ for all the sets.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i=3}^{\\infty }{Y}_{i}=(-\\infty ,0].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/